            <ArticleTitle>Respiratory failure as a complication of pharyngitis: Lemierre's syndrome.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>402-3</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The emergence of drug-resistant organisms has promoted increased calls for judicious use of antibiotics in cases of pediatric pharyngitis. Although these recommendations are largely justified, the case of a 16-year-old girl with pharyngitis is reported to alert readers to an unusual complication, Lemierre's syndrome. This complication of pharyngitis and its relevance to changing practice habits are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
